{"claims": [{"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:layout", "lean": ["Shape.layout"], "number": "Theorem 1", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:layout}\\lean{Shape.layout} Let $E$ be a nonempty type and $1 \\le j \\le k$. For every $x$ there is a constant $C$ such that, for every $n$, both $x \\le C$ and $n + x \\le n + C$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:witnesses", "lean": ["Shape.witnesses"], "number": "Theorem 2", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:witnesses}\\lean{Shape.witnesses} For every $j$ there is a function $x$ with $x(j) = j$ and $j \\le x(j)$, and there is a boolean $x$ that is true.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:shapes", "lean": ["Shape.shapes"], "number": "Theorem 3", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:shapes}\\lean{Shape.shapes} Let $E$ be nonempty. No natural number is negative, and either every $n$ satisfies $0 \\le n$ or, if $1 = 1$, some $m$ equals $1$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:def:multiple", "lean": ["Shape.MultipleAbove", "Shape.fib"], "number": "Definition 1", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{def:multiple}\\lean{Shape.MultipleAbove}\\lean{Shape.fib} A number $n$ is a multiple of $m$ above $b$ if $n = mq$ for some $q \\ge b$. The Fibonacci numbers are $F_0 = 0$, $F_1 = 1$ and $F_{n+2} = F_n + F_{n+1}$.", "status": "linked: Lean definition", "status_code": "link.definition", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:supplied", "lean": ["Shape.supplied"], "number": "Theorem 4", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:supplied}\\lean{Shape.supplied} Let $s$ be a solution for $d$ with bound at most $5$. Then $s$ starts at most at $5$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:assumed", "lean": ["Shape.assumed"], "number": "Theorem 5", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:assumed}\\lean{Shape.assumed} If every admissible datum has a good solution, then $0$ has a good solution.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:produced", "lean": ["Shape.produced"], "number": "Theorem 6", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:produced}\\lean{Shape.produced} Every admissible datum $d$ has a good solution.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:positive", "lean": ["Shape.positive"], "number": "Theorem 7", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:positive}\\lean{Shape.positive} Every positive number is at least $1$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:single", "lean": ["Shape.single"], "number": "Theorem 8", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:single}\\lean{Shape.single} A type with a single element has at most one element, and exactly one.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:probability", "lean": ["Shape.probability"], "number": "Theorem 9", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:probability}\\lean{Shape.probability} On a probability space, the whole space has measure one.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:none-large", "lean": ["Shape.none_large"], "number": "Theorem 10", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:none-large}\\lean{Shape.none_large} No solution for $0$ has a negative bound.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:both", "lean": ["Shape.both"], "number": "Theorem 11", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:both}\\lean{Shape.both} If $a \\le b$ and $b \\le a$, then $a = b$.", "statu